+1.1 For $r>0$, let $P_r$ be parallel transport along the arc $z(t)=re^{it}$, $0\le t\le\theta$, and put $M_r:=gP_r$, an endomorphism of the initial fiber. The connection form $\Omega=A(z)\,dz/z$ is flat on the punctured disk: holomorphicity gives $d\Omega=0$, and $\Omega\wedge\Omega=0$ because both factors are multiples of $dz$. Hence parallel transport around the boundary of an annular sector is the identity. If $r_1,r_2$ are two small radii, radial parallel transport identifies the initial fibers and the endpoint fibers; the coefficient identity in [F2] makes the resulting square commute with the endpoint identifications. Thus the two $M_r$ are conjugate and have the same characteristic polynomial. [F2, F3, given, algebra]
 
 1.2 Since $A(re^{it})\to R$ uniformly for $0\le t\le\theta$ as $r\to0$, subtract the integral equations for $P_r(t)$ and $e^{itR}$ from [F1]. The difference norm is bounded by $\int_0^t\|A(re^{iu})-R\|\,\|P_r(u)\|\,du+\int_0^t\|R\|\,\|P_r(u)-e^{iuR}\|\,du$; Grönwall's inequality gives $P_r(\theta)\to e^{i\theta R}$. Therefore $M_r\to g e^{i\theta R}$. [F1, F3, choose, algebra]
 
